74 "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(V),$ we reduce the matrix $V$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(V)$ is $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$" 13194139534509 17592186045417 true] [17592186423621 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423619 13194139534509 17592186045417 true] [17592186423621 1069 "q-75982" 13194139534509 17592186045417 true] [17592186423621 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534509 17592186045417 true] [17592186423621 1071 "The matrix $F$ is given below. Let ${f}_{1}$, ${f}_{2}$,  ${f}_{3}$ and ${f}_{4}$ be the respective columns of $F.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{f}_{1},{f}_{2},{f}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(F).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${f}_{4}={x}_{1}{f}_{1}+{x}_{2}{f}_{2}+{x}_{3}{f}_{3}.$ \n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 & -24 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534509 17592186045417 true] [17592186423621 1072 #uuid "693e6ed3-909b-52a6-8fa3-e0e6ae013327" 13194139534509 17592186045417 true] [17592186423621 1074 "First, we reduce the matrix $F$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 & -24 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(F)$ is $\\{{f}_{1},{f}_{2}\\}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B=\\{{f}_{1},{f}_{2},{f}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(F).$" 13194139534509 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0aa456ff-14e6-5b4c-8bb6-5fa53d7a73e7" 17592186423601 "answer-1b239761-1533-5b95-9abe-da3e7f8edb7a" 17592186423602 "answer-2b80385e-3a37-5b43-b815-d32cf7c3607c" 17592186423603 "answer-35e3091b-8980-52e7-a1d9-a90be4aa96ba" 17592186423604 "answer-3d86af19-6bb9-5da7-832b-79a566c84f6f" 17592186423605 "answer-67c52e20-2bf3-5d92-86ef-d45fa30e8513" 17592186423606 "answer-79611b73-f06c-516d-a314-79fc8a0df50a" 17592186423607 "answer-7ef60749-f0a3-5b92-b7ac-687d57c40bab" 17592186423608 "answer-842c1b53-7a3c-5c3c-95cd-f635e53b9e76" 17592186423609 "answer-8f1ff8c3-beef-5403-bf54-dedcfd80e6c8" 17592186423610 "answer-9f2e8bb6-fedc-5092-b791-68f16dc74270" 17592186423611 "answer-a9845672-a026-53af-b2ba-1e8d7af5f91b" 17592186423612 "answer-c1363c60-15a5-5bca-ae79-3b740d941738" 17592186423613 "answer-c62c345c-75b2-5956-a3af-45a35e4a85f2" 17592186423614 "answer-ca8dfba9-883e-5552-a0f0-cb69cf694e80" 17592186423615 "answer-ce207c25-42d3-5952-b1ac-04aeb42aad0c" 17592186423616 "answer-f635b87e-9ad6-595e-8ac8-cf7446521d1f" 17592186423617 "answer-field-8d734853-a228-557f-9012-a5d01ef1cf52" 17592186423618 "answer-field-f7f4cbcc-1506-5396-b835-9d7d9a6a3ab8" 17592186423619 "question-0c2bc939-4b4c-5161-9351-90818be5a0a1" 17592186423620 "question-693e6ed3-909b-5